marchyo NEWS                                             -*- outline -*-

User-visible changes worth mentioning, newest first, after the GNU
Coding Standards (NEWS File). marchyo has no releases, so changes are
grouped by year; CHANGELOG.md lists them in detail with commit links.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026

  More of omarchy's first-party shell plugins are packaged: workspaces,
  active window, tray, media, polkit, network, weather, tailscale,
  elsewhen and dropbox. A plugin can now replace a native panel or the
  polkit agent with `replaces`; native components stay the default.

  Theme switching keeps btop and the desktop light/dark preference on
  the same saved selection after a rebuild. A failed preference update
  reports an error and preserves the previous selection. Chrome,
  Chromium and Brave now follow the light/dark switch too.

** New features

  Web app preset marchyo.webapps.presets.google adds the Google
  Workspace apps: Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Meet,
  Chat, Keep, Forms, Sites, Contacts and Tasks.

  New panels: Bluetooth (Super+Ctrl+B), a speed test for network and
  disk (Super+Ctrl+Alt+P) and Dropbox (Super+Ctrl+Alt+D).  Breaking:
  Super+Ctrl+B used to start the bluetui manager; that is now
  Super+Ctrl+Shift+B while the shell is on.  The agents panel marks old
  limits as stale and tells you when an agent needs a sign-in, and
  display tiles in the Display panel work from the keyboard.

  Bar: the middle of the bar has three sections, so widgets can sit
  beside the clock without moving it.  The recording, reminder,
  remote session, dictation, stay-awake and do-not-disturb indicators
  form one group, and tray icons can be pinned so the rest fold behind
  the "·" button.  "marchyo bar put", "move", "remove" and "set" rearrange
  the bar without a rebuild, and "marchyo bar reset" undoes it.
  Double-click empty bar space to change the bar background.

  omarchy's menu, emoji picker and clipboard manager can replace the
  launcher: add omarchy-menu, omarchy-emojis and omarchy-clipboard to
  marchyo.shell.plugins.  Super+Space, Super+R, Super+K, Super+Ctrl+E
  and Super+Ctrl+V then open them, the menu shows marchyo.menu.entries,
  and "marchyo menu select" and "input" answer through omarchy's menu.

  Theme and wallpaper pickers: Super+Ctrl+T now opens a grid of theme
  previews instead of the launcher's theme mode, and Super+Ctrl+Shift+W
  opens the same grid for wallpapers.  Arrows move, Enter applies, Escape
  closes.  Marchyo draws four wallpaper patterns (grid, dots, bands,
  contour) per light and dark theme; "marchyo bg list" lists what you
  can choose, and a theme can list its own wallpapers.

  Fonts and appearance: "marchyo font set <family> --kind ui" changes the
  interface font of GTK and the shell as well as the terminal font.
  "marchyo theme gaps", "bar-position", "bar-background" and "icons" change
  window gaps, the bar placement, its background and the icon theme
  without a rebuild; the Control Center has an Appearance section for
  them.  Runtime theme, wallpaper, font and appearance changes now
  survive a rebuild until you revert them.

  More themed apps: btop, kitty, foot, alacritty, Helix, Neovim, Emacs
  and Chromium-based browsers follow the theme.  Browsers keep the
  colour of the theme built into the system.

  Command menu: Super+Space opens a searchable menu of everything
  marchyo can do (apps, capture, toggles, appearance, hardware, system,
  setup, share); Escape goes up a level.  Super+Alt+Space opens the
  apps, Super+K the keybinding cheat sheet.  Add or hide entries with
  marchyo.menu.entries or ~/.config/marchyo/menu.local.json.  Breaking
  binds: the browser, file manager and messenger moved to Super+Shift+B,
  Super+Shift+F and Super+Shift+G (marchyo.keyboard.legacyBinds keeps
  the old chords), and Super+Alt+Space no longer opens the gum menu.

  Shell plugins: panel, menu, overlay, service and bar plugins from
  omarchy now run on the shell, with the omarchy-* helper commands they
  call.  "marchyo plugin validate" checks a plugin checkout.  On a
  development host, marchyo.shell.devPlugins.enable and "marchyo plugin
  dev" load a checkout without a rebuild; dev plugins are unreviewed
  code, so leave the option off elsewhere.

  Shell panels: panels opened with a key or "marchyo shell open" take
  keyboard focus.  Escape closes, Up, Down and Tab move between
  controls, Enter and Space activate.  The shell also has a native Ui
  kit and a dev gallery ("marchyo shell gallery") that shows it.

  Reduce motion at run time: "marchyo toggle reduce-motion on" makes
  every shell transition instant, and the shell follows Hyprland's
  animations setting.

  Crash diagnosis: when one of your programs dumps core, a notification
  offers to start your AI agent on the crash, with a skill that covers
  coredumpctl, NixOS debuginfo and reporting.  "marchyo toggle
  crash-capture off" silences it.  The marchyo, marchyo-plugin and
  diagnose-crash skills are installed for Claude Code, Codex and opencode.

  Dev environments: "marchyo dev init <lang>" writes a devenv.nix,
  devenv.yaml and .envrc for the language into the current directory,
  and "marchyo dev db <engine>" adds a database service (postgres,
  mysql, mariadb, redis or mongodb) to an existing devenv.nix.

  Notifications from scripts: "marchyo notify" takes the flags of
  omarchy-notification-send and can attach a click command and up to three
  buttons.  Toasts that were on screen come back after a shell restart,
  do-not-disturb is kept across restarts, and the notification centre
  works from the keyboard (Up, Down, Enter, Delete).  Only
  "marchyo notify" can attach a click command: each one carries a
  one-time token, and the shell checks it again when a notification is
  replaced.

  What changed and first-login setup: when Marchyo's NEWS changed, one
  notification opens a panel with the new entries and a summary of the
  last switch.  On the first login a welcome notification opens a setup
  checklist ("marchyo setup") for git, SSH, FIDO2, fingerprint, language,
  keyboard, theme, agent login and dictation.  Super+Ctrl+U and
  Super+Ctrl+H open the two panels.

  Notifications: toasts stack by sender into decks that expand on
  hover, show verification codes with a Copy button, and route clicks
  to the sender's window or link.  Do-not-disturb still lets through
  critical notifications, Marchyo's own and those carrying a code.

  Display panel: a shell panel (global shortcut panel.display) for
  each display's brightness, scale, resolution, refresh rate and
  rotation, with a layout map to drag displays around and Extend or
  Mirror for the laptop panel.  Choices are kept per monitor in
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/marchyo/monitors/settings and survive rebuilds.
  "marchyo monitor reset" clears them, "marchyo monitor save --nix"
  prints the layout as marchyo.monitors, and
  marchyo.monitorPanel.persist = false ignores the file.

  Per-monitor workspaces: every monitor has its own workspaces 1-10,
  and Super+1..0 act on the focused monitor.  A monitor keeps its
  workspaces across unplugs, and the bar numbers each monitor's
  workspaces from 1.  Set marchyo.workspaces.perMonitor = false for
  one global set; "marchyo monitor workspaces reset" starts over.

  Agent accounts: "marchyo agent account add claude Work" signs in a
  second Claude Code, Codex or Grok account.  History, settings and
  sessions stay shared, so "claude --continue" works after a switch.
  "marchyo agent account use" picks the account for new sessions; at a
  usage threshold marchyo offers a switch, or switches by itself in
  auto mode.  "marchyo agent account copy <host>" moves the sign-ins
  to another machine over ssh.

  AI agent usage: marchyo.ai.agents installs agent CLIs, and the
  agents panel and the marchyo.agents bar widget show the Claude Code,
  Codex and GitHub Copilot usage limits with their reset times.
  "marchyo agent usage" prints the same data with token totals.

  Agent console: marchyo.console adds a Quake-style terminal on
  Super+Ctrl+grave that starts the default AI agent.  marchyo.ai.herdr
  and marchyo.ai.amp install herdr and the Amp apps.

  World clock and status indicators: the Elsewhen panel (Super+Ctrl+Alt+E)
  shows the time in your cities on a map.  Optional bar indicators show a
  connected gliff remote session, a pending update, a nearly full Nix
  store disk (marchyo.shell.diskWarnPercent) and failing "marchyo doctor"
  checks.  The Power panel can roll back to the previous generation.

  Window appearance: marchyo.theme.appearance.transparency (opaque,
  transparent, glassy), corners (theme, sharp, rounded) and animations
  (auto, on, off) set how windows look.  "marchyo theme transparency",
  "marchyo theme corners" and "marchyo toggle animations" switch them
  live, and the Appearance menu groups them with theme, background and
  font.  "marchyo window pop" (Super+Alt+O) pops a tile out as a
  floating pinned window.

  Peripherals: marchyo.audio.tuner applies a laptop speaker tuning,
  marchyo.hardware.camlink relays an Elgato Cam Link 4K as a virtual
  camera, and WirePlumber now waits at login for camera access.
  "marchyo share --tailscale <peer>" sends files over Taildrop.

  Theme surfaces: "marchyo theme" now also themes VS Code (and
  Insiders, VSCodium, Cursor), Obsidian, tmux, fcitx5 and herdr.
  marchyo.tmux.enable (on with marchyo.development.enable) gives a
  themed tmux, and marchyo.slack.themeInjection.enable themes Slack
  through an opt-in launcher.
  Display language: marchyo.language (derived from
  marchyo.defaultLocale) sets the language of the shell and CLI
  strings, and "marchyo language <code>" switches it live.  Missing
  translations fall back to English.
  Captive portals: NetworkManager now checks connectivity against
  nmcheck.gnome.org by default on desktops (marchyo.network.connectivityCheck;
  set enable = false to send no probes).  The shell marks restricted
  networks, and "marchyo network portal" or the Network panel opens the
  sign-in page.
  Power: marchyo.power.hibernation turns hibernation back on, with
  suspend-then-hibernate and a resume-device assertion.  marchyo.power.lid
  sets the lid-close action on battery, on AC and when docked.  Closing
  the lid with an external display connected turns the laptop panel off.
  Input methods: marchyo.keyboard.layouts accepts the ime values
  chewing (Zhuyin) and cangjie (Cangjie 5).  Input starts in Latin; a
  lone Shift toggles the engine and Super+I cycles layouts, then
  engines.  Noto CJK fonts follow the configured language.
  Keyboard: marchyo.keyboard.fnMode picks whether the top row sends
  media keys or F1-F12 by default, the keyboard backlight keys work
  through "marchyo brightness --keyboard", and composeKey can be
  "shift-caps" (Shift+Caps Lock composes, Caps Lock stays Caps Lock).

  GPU options: marchyo.graphics.nvidia selects the driver branch and
  GPU generation and enables the NVIDIA Container Toolkit with
  development containers.  marchyo.graphics.amd adds ROCm, VA-API and
  overdrive.  Hybrid laptops can add an "integrated-only" boot entry
  that turns the NVIDIA GPU off.

  Local models: marchyo.ai.local runs Ollama with the build that
  matches the GPU and registers it as an opencode provider.

  The fleet and options UI is available at marchyo.org/os. It stores
  configuration in the browser and exports Nix configuration.

  Web app presets: marchyo.webapps.presets.m365 adds Outlook, Word,
  Excel, PowerPoint, Teams and OneDrive, and presets.notion adds Notion.

  Quickshell desktop shell: marchyo.shell provides a bar, launcher
  command palette, notification centre, Control Center, workspace
  overview, session lock and greeter in one themed shell.  It is
  enabled by default with marchyo.desktop.enable and replaces waybar,
  mako, SwayOSD and Vicinae.

  marchyo CLI: a 1.0 command line with a frozen command surface for
  theme, toggle, capture, update, rollback, gc, diff, doctor, share,
  plugin and more, with shell completions and a man page.  Changes
  apply to the running desktop and are restored at startup.

  Runtime theming: themes switch live without a rebuild across the
  shell, Ghostty, Hyprland, GTK, Qt, bat, fzf, hyprlock and the console,
  and "marchyo theme generate" derives a palette from a wallpaper.

  Omarchy-style desktop: central and power menus, dictation with
  Whisper, web apps with launch keys, screensaver, do-not-disturb,
  caffeine, fingerprint and FIDO2 login, and shell plugins that run
  upstream omarchy Quickshell plugins.

  Typed options: marchyo.monitors, marchyo.defaults, marchyo.identity,
  marchyo.nix.caches and marchyo.theme.fontScale and appearance, plus
  GPU vendor and NVIDIA PRIME settings, system builders for NixOS
  and nix-on-droid.

  Documentation: a Starlight site with an end-user manual and
  searchable option and package reference.

** Changes in behavior

  Compose key: marchyo.keyboard.composeKey defaults to "shift-caps",
  so Shift+Caps Lock is Compose in Hyprland and Caps Lock stays Caps
  Lock.  The console and X get no compose key; set "menu" to keep the
  Menu key.

  Hotkeys (breaking): the Hyprland binds follow the Omarchy 4.5
  planes.  Super is the system, Super+Shift apps, Super+Ctrl panels
  and menus, Super+Ctrl+Alt quick actions.  Set
  marchyo.keyboard.legacyBinds = true to keep the old layout for one
  release.  Moved binds, old -> new:

    Lock                       Super+L -> Super+Ctrl+L
    Music player               Super+M -> Super+Shift+M
    Audio panel                Super+Shift+V -> Super+Ctrl+A
    Network panel              Super+Shift+N -> Super+Ctrl+N
    Power panel                Super+Shift+B -> Super+Ctrl+P
    System monitor panel       Super+Shift+M -> Super+Ctrl+M
    Control Center             Super+Shift+Q -> Super+Ctrl+O
    Window overview            Super+grave -> Super+Ctrl+grave
    Quake console              Super+Ctrl+grave -> Super+grave
    Window to Quake console    Super+Ctrl+Shift+grave -> Super+Shift+grave
    Emoji picker               Super+period -> Super+Ctrl+E
    Dismiss all notifications  Super+Ctrl+Shift+comma -> Super+Shift+comma
    Notification history       Super+N -> Super+Shift+Alt+comma
    Notification keyboard      Super+Alt+comma -> Super+Ctrl+comma
    Do-not-disturb             Super+Ctrl+comma -> Super+Ctrl+Alt+comma
    Emacs everywhere           Super+Ctrl+E -> Super+Shift+Alt+E
    Org capture                Super+Shift+T -> Super+Ctrl+Alt+O
    Emacs-aware focus/swap     Super+Alt(+Shift)+H/J/K/L
                               -> Super+Ctrl+Alt(+Shift)+H/J/K/L
    Window to monitor          Super+Shift+comma/period
                               -> Super+Shift+Ctrl+arrows

  New binds: Super+L / Super+Alt+L cycle the workspace layout
  (dwindle, scrolling, master), Super+M minimizes to the drawer,
  Super+A selects all, Super+comma acts on the newest notification
  and Super+Alt+comma dismisses it, Super+Shift+Q calculator (qalc),
  Super+Shift+T activity (btop), Super+Ctrl+D display panel,
  Super+Shift+Ctrl+A agents panel, Super+Ctrl+W next background,
  Super+Ctrl+Alt+C screenshot and Super+Ctrl+Alt+F full screen
  desktop.  Super+C and Super+V send Ctrl+Shift+C/V in terminals and
  keep Ctrl+Insert/Shift+Insert elsewhere.  Removed: the night light bind (Super+Ctrl+N)
  and the nmtui bind on Super+Ctrl+W; without the shell,
  Super+Ctrl+A and Super+Ctrl+N open wiremix and nmtui.  Super+K
  lists the binds from the same table.

  Translations: the whole shell and the runtime messages and menus of
  the marchyo command follow marchyo.language.  Strings without a
  translation in your language show in English.

  Dictation backend: marchyo.dictation.backend now defaults to
  superwhisper, a proprietary (unfree) program that needs
  nixpkgs.config.allowUnfree.  Set it to "voxtype" to keep the old
  open-source engine, or "hex".  Alt+Space toggles recording
  (previously Super+Ctrl+X); F9 stays push-to-talk.

  Faster menus and panels: the shell's keybinds reach it through
  Hyprland global shortcuts, and marchyo CLI calls through a private
  unix socket, so no process starts per keypress.

  Faster logout, reboot and shutdown: marchyo closes every window and
  waits at most two seconds for the apps before it ends the session.

  BBR congestion control with the fq qdisc is now the default on every
  host, not only with marchyo.performance.tuning.  Non-rotational disks
  use the kyber I/O scheduler; with tuning.nvme, NVMe disks keep
  mq-deadline.  marchyo.security.ssh adds a key-only SSH server that
  refuses to evaluate while a login user has no authorized key.

  Ghostty is the default terminal, bash the only login shell, and the
  design system moved to a Jost, Fira Sans and IBM Plex Mono look.
  Development tools default to rootless Podman, and the default
  keyboard layout is us(altgr-intl) with Compose on the Menu key.

  Security defaults tightened: CPU mitigations stay on unless
  marchyo.performance.disableMitigations is set, accept-flake-config is
  no longer enabled, users no longer join the docker group by default,
  and the cache proxy listens on localhost only.

  The systemd-boot menu is hidden by default. Hold Space at power-on to
  open it, or set boot.loader.timeout to show it.

  OBS Studio and lazydocker are no longer installed. The SUPER + ALT + D
  lazydocker bind is removed too. Add the packages through
  environment.systemPackages if you want them.

** Removed features

  Stylix, nix-darwin support, the Vicinae, noctalia, waybar, mako and
  SwayOSD modules, the self-tracking telemetry stack and the marchyo.ai
  BYOK tooling were removed.  The gaming, kmscon, snapper and
  hibernation modules gave way to upstream NixOS options.

  The search demo page at marchyo.org/search was removed.  The fleet app at marchyo.org/os
  no longer has packages and options pages.

** Bug fixes

  Fixed Hyprland Lua-config breakage, shell and greeter crash loops,
  the black login screen, dconf conflicts on light-theme rebuilds and
  Qt 6.12 turning shell colours black.

* Noteworthy changes in 2025

** New features

  First version of the NixOS and Home Manager module set for a
  Hyprland desktop, with marchyo.* options for users and desktop,
  development, media and office feature flags.

  Installation tooling: installer ISOs, disko layouts, workstation and
  minimal flake templates, and marchyo.lib.mkNixosSystem.

  Theming through nix-colors Base16 schemes with the Modus schemes, and
  fcitx5 input methods with Chinese, Japanese and Korean support under
  marchyo.keyboard.layouts.

  Optional sops-nix secrets, Prometheus and Grafana monitoring, system
  hardening and BTRFS root rollback.

** Changes in behavior

  The legacy base, desktop and developer profiles were removed;
  desktop and development settings now follow their enable options.
